> Explain the difference between RAM and storage in three sentences.
RAM is volatile memory that provides fast, temporary workspace for active programs and data, losing its contents when power is turned off. Storage is non-volatile memory that permanently retains files, applications, and the operating system even without power. While RAM determines how many tasks a computer can handle simultaneously, storage determines the total capacity of data that can be saved long-term.

